/**
 * The `stroke-linejoin` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines
 * the shape to be used at the corners of an [SVG](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG)
 * element's stroked paths. If present, it overrides the element's `stroke-linejoin` attribute.
 *
 * Initial: miter. Inherited: yes.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - arcs: _(Unsupported.)_ Indicates that an _arcs corner_ is to be used to join path segments. The
 * arc's shape is formed by extending the outer edges of the stroke at the join point with arcs that
 * have the same curvature as the outer edges at the join point.
 * - bevel: Indicates that a beveled corner is to be used to join path segments. The bevel is formed
 * by truncating the corner by a line perpendicular to a line that bisects the difference in the
 * subpath angles where they meet the join point.
 * - miter: Indicates that a sharp corner is to be used to join path segments. The corner is formed
 * by extending the outer edges of the stroke at the tangents of the path segments until they
 * intersect. This is the default value.
 * - round: Indicates that a round corner is to be used to join path segments. This is accomplished
 * by cropping the join as per `bevel`, and then appending a filled arc tangent in order to round
 * the corner.
 *
 * Grammar: [ crop | arcs | miter ] || [ bevel | round | fallback ]
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/fill-stroke-3/#propdef-stroke-linejoin
 *
 * Author guide:
